{
  "schema_version": "prompt-runtime.program-scenario.v1",
  "story_path": "user_stories/approval-policy-ports.md",
  "criteria": [
    {
      "id": "AC1",
      "text": "`readApprovalPolicy` reads `pdd.json` in `root`, returning `{strictApprovals: true}` when `strict_approvals` is `true`, `{strictApprovals: false}` when the file or key is absent, and raising `invalid-approval-policy` when `pdd.json` is malformed or has a non-boolean `strict_approvals`."
    },
    {
      "id": "AC2",
      "text": "`readSaidWords` reads once from `stdin.read` when `said` is `-`, preserves verbatim text including newlines and quotes, and raises `invalid-said-words` when the payload is blank-only."
    },
    {
      "id": "AC3",
      "text": "`approvalActor` prefers `CODEX_THREAD_ID` over `PDD_AGENT_SESSION`, falls back to terminal `USER` or `LOGNAME`, and raises `invalid-actor-env` when an environment value contains NUL."
    },
    {
      "id": "AC4",
      "text": "`readPromptApprovals` returns retained journal records from `pdd/approvals.json` under `commonDir` and raises `invalid-approval-journal` when the existing file is malformed."
    },
    {
      "id": "AC5",
      "text": "`recordPromptApproval` acquires lock custody, invokes `guards.afterApprovalLock` and `guards.beforeApprovalCommit`, allocates an event ID when absent, writes the updated `{v: 1, approvals}` journal, releases the lock, and raises `guard-refused` without writing when a guard rejects."
    }
  ],
